From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Dylan Ironside <dylan@dylanironside.io>
Date: Sat, 14 Nov 2026 18:43:13 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] drm/asahi: G16: admit twice as many jobs per queue as
 it has units

With eight compute units and up to seven compute commands allowed
behind a running one, 71 % of the J604's compute commands still found
the firmware idle (1.910, compute.light 84.8 us per submit). A queue's
scheduler admitted as many jobs as its resident render units (eight):
exactly the compute units. A credit only returns when a job's fence
signals at host retirement, so the next job reached the engine only
after a full round trip, and the queued slots refilled late.

Admit twice the larger of the latched resident render units and
compute units, so the next jobs are already waiting when a unit frees.
The engine's own limits (units, g16_horizon, g16_resident) still bound
what is published; only admission moves earlier. The stats "gaps" and
"starved_us" lines tell a firmware gap with work ready from a client
that was late.

Assisted-by: LLM
Signed-off-by: Dylan Ironside <dylan@dylanironside.io>
---
 drivers/gpu/drm/asahi/g16/params.rs | 11 +++++++----
 1 file changed, 7 insertions(+), 4 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/asahi/g16/params.rs b/drivers/gpu/drm/asahi/g16/params.rs
index 67f7660e4e..3c691d0f6b 100644
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/asahi/g16/params.rs
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/asahi/g16/params.rs
@@ -1102,11 +1102,14 @@ pub(crate) fn resident() -> usize {
     v.min(resident_units()).min(hw::sizes::FLIGHTS)
 }
 
-/// Scheduler credits of a queue created now: [`hw::sizes::SCHEDULER_CREDITS`], or the
-/// latched resident units when larger, so `g16_resident` jobs of one queue can be admitted
-/// together.
+/// Scheduler credits of a queue created now: twice the larger of the latched resident render
+/// units and the latched compute units (at least [`hw::sizes::SCHEDULER_CREDITS`]), so a
+/// queue's next jobs are already admitted while its units are full: a credit only returns
+/// when a job's fence signals at host retirement, and with credits equal to the units the
+/// next job reached the engine only after that (1.910: 71 % of compute commands found the
+/// firmware idle with all 8 units free).
 pub(crate) fn resident_credits() -> u32 {
-    (resident_units() as u32).max(hw::sizes::SCHEDULER_CREDITS)
+    (2 * resident_units().max(compute_units()) as u32).max(hw::sizes::SCHEDULER_CREDITS)
 }
 
 live_u32_param!(
